error[type.mismatch]: an operand of `Meters` meets `int` — a named type never mixes with its shape
  ╭─[<case>/src/main.av:2:42]
2 │ fn f(m: Meters, k: int) -> Meters { m + (k * 2) }
  ·                                          ┬
  ·                                          ╰── this is `int`
──╯
help: `Meters` is its own type — a value of its shape crosses by construction
fix (high): write `Meters(k * 2)`
  Meters(k * 2)
